= Using the locale class =

* [#intro Introduction]
* [#categories Locale Categories]
* [#numeric Numeric Formatting]
* [#monetary Monetary Formatting]


[=#intro]
== Introduction ==

The [../classes/html/classlocale.html locale class] provides static methods for accessing and manipulating locale categories.

Locale categories control various aspects of how programs format numbers, currency, dates, and other locale-sensitive data.


[=#categories]
== Locale Categories ==

The locale class provides methods for getting and setting standard locale categories such as LC_ALL, LC_COLLATE, LC_CTYPE, LC_MESSAGES, LC_MONETARY, LC_NUMERIC, and LC_TIME.  Additional categories such as LC_ADDRESS, LC_IDENTIFICATION, LC_MEASUREMENT, LC_NAME, LC_PAPER, and LC_TELEPHONE are also supported, where available.

Each category has a set/get pair and an isSupported method.


[=#numeric]
== Numeric Formatting ==

Methods are provided for getting the numeric decimal point string, digit group separator, and digit group counts for the current locale.


[=#monetary]
== Monetary Formatting ==

Methods are provided for getting monetary formatting information including the decimal point, digit group separator, currency symbol, positive/negative signs, sign positions, and the number of decimal digits for both local and international formats.

